  "title": "The Tale of Genji",
  "summary": "The Tale of Genji is a long Heian-period court narrative by Murasaki Shikibu, regarded as Japan's oldest novel. She wrote it while serving Empress Shoshi, and her diary of 1008–1010 shows it circulating at court. Sources date its completion differently, from around 1012 to around 1020.",
